From 5cd405edc0089f89a4afdd620216e2a4f5071f52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:33:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: 60-second blitz quiz

A new mode: as many flags as you can name in one minute. It runs against a single clock that starts with
the quiz and that answering never stops; after each answer the next flag follows by itself after 0.8
seconds (the Next button is still there). Flags come from successive shuffles of the scope, so no country
repeats before every other has and none ever follows itself, and look-alike answers follow the chosen
difficulty like every flag question. A blitz that is still on its first question when the minute ends
costs nothing: no review is recorded for the unanswered flag.

The score screen says Time's up! with the number right and the points. A blitz is saved with its points in
score and the number of right answers in total (a fixed-length quiz keeps its best possible score there),
the Progress log shows it as N correct and points, and it is left out of Highest Score, where a long run
would swamp the 190-point maximum of the other modes.

